;; India (Central Government offices, Delhi/New Delhi) national holidays 2002-2040: external gold for IN.
;; Regenerate: uv run --no-project --with holidays==0.109 python -I scripts/generate_asia_holiday_gold.py IN
;; :days lists every holiday as (YEAR MONTH DAY NAME); any other day is not one.
(
 :country "IN"
 :generated "2026-11-27"
 :from 2002 :to 2040
 :note "Gazetted holidays of the administrative offices of the Central Government located at Delhi/New Delhi: Annexure-I of each year's DoPT Office Memorandum (the 14 compulsory holidays and the 3 DoPT selects from the 12 optional ones), with the later O.M.s that move an Islamic holiday after the moon is sighted or declare a further holiday (Dr B. R. Ambedkar's birthday, the 2010 Commonwealth Games closing day, the 2023 G-20 closing day). 2002-2004 and 2007-2027 are O.M. years; 2005 and 2006 are not checked (:gaps: no copy of the O.M. was found). 2028-2040 are provisional: the fixed days, Good Friday and tabular estimates of the four Islamic holidays, with no Hindu, Sikh, Jain or Buddhist day. :restricted lists Annexure-II, of which each employee may take two; they are not office closures. Holidays that fall on a Saturday or Sunday are listed: the O.M.s allow no substitute (para 3.2)."
 :gaps (2005 2006)
